 "body_html": "<p>“Predicting the future is not so hard\"; “people keep meta frameworks in mind surprisingly rarely\"; “<a href=\"https://croissanthology.com/fruit\">it's a good idea to</a> list out your tentative priors about the world\"; “spit out ideas on Substack and see how quickly you get lambasted for them to learn QUICKLY\"; “invest in the conversation with Claude from 22 days ago squatting on the floor of a bookstore —&gt; public posts pipeline\"; “what does a non-<a href=\"https://www.lesswrong.com/w/gears-level\">gears-level-model</a> of the world look like?”; “how good can your world model be if it relies on a bunch of black box intuitions?”; “people keep being surprised when these priors are wrong\".</p><p>In other words, I'm going to say a few fairly outrageous things, tack on empirical observations, and made absolutely no local efforts to discovering why the world works like this. This is Tentative Priors About the World!</p><p><strong>If a technology exists, it gets cheaper over time.</strong> </p><p>Similar to “when a technology is <em>feasible</em> in small quantities, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assembly_line\">it's feasible in large quantities</a>\"; “when <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_motor\">one variable interfacing with another</a> can be affected, you can <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_generator\">interface with the other variable</a> (see at its simplest: the shape of a wind turbine is similar to the shape of an airplane propeller)”; “<a href=\"https://x.com/croissanthology/status/1961232736842064035?s=20\">having a grip on a physical law is often enough to extract technology out of it</a>\". </p><p>Examples: </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-tkG!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F67a3dfc7-abb9-4cb8-995e-7c1e5ec2def6_2160x2160.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-tkG!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F67a3dfc7-abb9-4cb8-995e-7c1e5ec2def6_2160x2160.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-tkG!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F67a3dfc7-abb9-4cb8-995e-7c1e5ec2def6_2160x2160.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-tkG!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F67a3dfc7-abb9-4cb8-995e-7c1e5ec2def6_2160x2160.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-tkG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F67a3dfc7-abb9-4cb8-995e-7c1e5ec2def6_2160x2160.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-tkG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F67a3dfc7-abb9-4cb8-995e-7c1e5ec2def6_2160x2160.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1456\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/67a3dfc7-abb9-4cb8-995e-7c1e5ec2def6_2160x2160.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1456,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;A connected scatterplot showing the cost of solar PV measured against cumulative installed capacity. Prices have fallen exponentially: by 20% for every doubling in installed capacity.&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:fa