l,&quot;height&quot;:1028,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:677114,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://croissanthology.substack.com/i/179214245?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0a830fdf-9ecd-44bc-9563-a2ed8c49c378_3400x2400.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0zMK!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0a830fdf-9ecd-44bc-9563-a2ed8c49c378_3400x2400.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0zMK!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0a830fdf-9ecd-44bc-9563-a2ed8c49c378_3400x2400.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0zMK!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0a830fdf-9ecd-44bc-9563-a2ed8c49c378_3400x2400.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0zMK!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0a830fdf-9ecd-44bc-9563-a2ed8c49c378_3400x2400.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\"><a href=\"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/gpu-price-performance\">Our World in Data</a></figcaption></figure></div><p>P(a given technology gets cheaper over time | it exists)≈1 feels like a strong prior to me, in the sense that if there are ~100 technologies that future historians might bother drawing maps about, I <em>would</em> make money betting that they would become cheaper.</p><p>But P(a given technology gets cheaper over time | it exists and is highly regulated for some reason) is going to be much farther away from 1. Nuclear power, for instance. </p><p>Market pressure, i.e. demand, seems to be a huge driver of technologies getting cheaper. So if you want to make the prior a little more precise, it's “if this technology exists and is exposed to a lot of market demand, it gets cheaper over time\". </p><p>In general, I think this prior holds. </p><p></p><div><hr></div><p></p><p><strong>Why is it not more common in people's world models?</strong> (In my experience, it is.) Why are people consistently registering surprise about solar panels being the cheapest form of marginal energy installation in 2025? What's so crazy about compute/intelligence becoming too-cheap-to-meter in a matter of years?</p><p>Perhaps because it's easy to get caught in an ambient sensation of impossibility, “this is really fucking hard\", man-in-the-arena-like difficulty of pushing the technological frontier. </p><p>After all, while technological progress / cheapness has continued at steady rates throughout all of history, from the <em>inside</em> the feeling is ever-decreasing rates of insights-per-hour, breakthroughs-per-dollar, understanding-of-the-whole-by-the-part:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"906\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/cea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:906,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:299760,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://croissanthology.substack.com/i/179214245?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0WH2!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcea27113-8641-4063-91c2-5761b04a71b9_1610x1002.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\"><a href=\"https://web.stanford.edu/~chadj/IdeaPF.pdf\">Paper link</a></figcaption></figure></div><p>Indeed,<a href=\"https://slatestarcodex.com/2018/11/26/is-science-slowing-down-2/\"> science-per-unit is slowing down.</a> </p><p>Hence Twitter vibes along the lines of “deep learning is hitting a wall” or “GPT-4.5 is the largest pre-training run ever but they stopped using it months after its release that must mean pre-training is hitting a wall” or “Grok 4 proves RL does not scale well\". </p><p>Hence also the difficulty of imagining how something so complex as a handheld game console in 1989 could ever be driven down to a reasonable price. And yet, if you're an outside observer (e.g. if you live somewhere after the year 1989), the prior holds. </p><div id=\"youtube2-BKm45Az02YE\" class=\"youtube-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;videoId&quot;:&quot;BKm45Az02YE&quot;,&quot;startTime&quot;:null,&quot;endTime&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"Youtube2ToDOM\"><div class=\"youtube-inner\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/BKm45Az02YE?rel=0&amp;autoplay=0&amp;showinfo=0&amp;enablejsapi=0\" frameborder=\"0\" loading=\"lazy\" gesture=\"media\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen\" allowautoplay=\"true\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" width=\"728\" height=\"409\"></iframe></div></div><p>(If you're on the inside, it might hold too, but <a href=\"http://v\">do not overrate the utility of your own observations.</a> And the amount of sweat it'll cost you to e.g. make the GameBoy cheap will detract you <em>constantly</em> from the correct conclusion that it'll “merely take a year” to do so.)</p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p>"
}
